<%# The baseline picker — one form per lineage hop (#911, generalised in #928).

    #911 put this inline in the reconciliation banner, where it is only reachable
    while the document is BLOCKED. That left two states with no way to declare a
    baseline at all:

      * a document that references no controls yet — `lineage_issues` is empty by
        design, so no banner renders, so an imported profile with zero controls
        had no picker, no publish button and no way forward;
      * a document already linked to the WRONG catalog — reconciled, so the
        banner is gone, and the only remaining remedy was the API.

    Both were reachable from the normal import order (upload the baseline before
    the catalog it derives from). The form is the same either way, so it lives
    here and both callers render it rather than growing a second implementation
    that can drift from the gate's idea of a lineage-resolving write.

    Posts to `set_baseline`, which permits exactly
    `lineage_attribute_names` — the same attributes the reconciliation gate
    accepts as resolving. A parallel path through `update_metadata` would be
    refused by that gate for an unreconciled document, which is the trap this is
    supposed to open.

    Locals:
      document      — any model including CatalogLineage
      submit_label  — button text (default "Set baseline")
      empty_notice  — false to drop the "nothing is loaded" prose (the caller
                      may already be saying it in its own words)
%>
<% submit_label = local_assigns.fetch(:submit_label, "Set baseline") %>
<% show_empty_notice = local_assigns.fetch(:empty_notice, true) %>

<% document.lineage_choices.each do |choice| %>
  <% if choice[:records].any? %>
    <%= form_with url: url_for(action: :set_baseline, id: document),
                  method: :patch, local: true,
                  class: "d-flex align-items-center gap-2 flex-wrap mb-2" do |f| %>
      <label class="fw-semibold mb-0" for="baseline_<%= choice[:attribute] %>">
        <%= choice[:label] %>
      </label>
      <%# Pre-select what is already set, so this reads as "change it" on a
          reconciled document and as "choose one" on an unreconciled one,
          without the caller having to know which state it is in. %>
      <%= select_tag "#{document.model_name.param_key}[#{choice[:attribute]}]",
            options_from_collection_for_select(choice[:records], :id, :name,
                                               document.public_send(choice[:attribute])),
            include_blank: "Choose a #{choice[:label].downcase}…",
            id: "baseline_#{choice[:attribute]}",
            class: "form-select form-select-sm w-auto" %>
      <%= f.submit submit_label, class: "btn btn-primary btn-sm" %>
    <% end %>
  <% elsif show_empty_notice %>
    <%# SPARC never invents a baseline from the document's own controls —
        that would validate the document against itself. When nothing
        suitable is loaded, say so plainly and name the remedy. %>
    <p class="mb-2">
      <strong>No <%= choice[:label].downcase %> is loaded to choose from.</strong>
      SPARC will not create one from this document's own controls — that would
      check the document against itself. Load the correct
      <%= choice[:label].downcase %> first, then set it here.
    </p>
  <% end %>
<% end %>
